4.3.147
Formulas for Solution of Plane Right Triangles
If A, B and C are the vertices (C the right angle), and a, b and c the sides opposite respectively,
\sin A=\frac{a}{c}=\frac{1}{\csc A}
\cos A=\frac{b}{c}=\frac{1}{\sec A}
\tan A=\frac{a}{b}=\frac{1}{\cot A}
\text{versine }A=\text{vers }A=1-\cos A
\text{coverse }A=\text{covers }A=\text{covers }A=1-\sin A
\text{haversine }A=\text{hav }A=\frac{1}{2}\text{vers }A
\text{exsecant }A=\text{exec }A=\text{see }A-1